{
  "assumptions": [
    "The s5_frozen file slots are produced by the s5 template/mechanical generation layer and are not owned by s6 modules; modules and work packages own only the s6_owned implementation files.",
    "The target profile is server-only; client-facing packet encoders are still owned by the codec module because conformance tests compare their bytes against Paho MQTT 3.1.1.",
    "The release and san build variants differ only in compiler flags and sanitizer support, not in protocol behavior or module boundaries.",
    "s5-ready contracts are owned and provided by the special s5 generation layer, so no work package needs to provide them and no work-package dependency is required for contract consumption."
  ],
